WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.170
Let's add one half and one third.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.610
The whole bars are the same size, but the pieces are different sizes.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.900
First, make equal pieces.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.420
Six is a common multiple of two and three.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.210
One half equals three sixths.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.920
One third equals two sixths.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.540
Now add three sixths and two sixths.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.550
Three plus two is five.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:39.090
The pieces are still sixths, so the denominator stays six.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.310
One half plus one third equals five sixths.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.170
We changed the size of the pieces, not the amount shaded.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:53.920
Try adding one half and one sixth yourself.
